# Curated L1 truth: the first real slice of what this organization does.
#
# Everything below is something the organization declared about itself, in the
# language it uses to say it. It is true because it was declared and reviewed, and it
# stays true until the organization declares otherwise. Nothing here was read out of a
# system, and nothing here decays.
#
# The slice is deliberately small: one outcome, the one thing the organization does to
# reach it, who answers for that, the agent it is delegated to, what that agent is
# permitted to do, the rule it works under, and the work itself. That is the whole
# chain an audit walks, and it is written here once end to end rather than sketched
# across several half-modelled areas.
#
# It names no repository, no branch, no queue, no command and no tool. Those are
# technical facts, they are only true as of the last time somebody looked, and business
# truth must not acquire an expiry date it has no way to honour. Which system happens to
# deliver the capability below is said in L2, by a single upward edge, and is not said
# here.

@prefix biz:    <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/biz#> .
@prefix goal:   <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/biz/goal/> .
@prefix cap:    <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/biz/capability/> .
@prefix person: <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/biz/person/> .
@prefix agent:  <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/biz/agent/> .
@prefix role:   <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/biz/role/> .
@prefix policy: <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/biz/policy/> .
@prefix asg:    <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/biz/assignment/> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

## The outcome.

goal:accountable-delegation-with-peace-of-mind
    a biz:Goal ;
    rdfs:label "Accountable delegation with peace of mind" ;
    rdfs:comment """What the captain asks for becomes an outcome they can rely on without having to
supervise how it was produced. Delegation that has to be watched is not delegation, and an outcome
nobody answers for is not one worth having, so both halves are the goal rather than one of them.""" .

## What the organization does about it.

cap:orchestrate-fleet-delivery
    a biz:Capability ;
    rdfs:label "Orchestrate fleet delivery" ;
    rdfs:comment """Turning the captain's intent into work that is bounded before it starts, accepted
independently of whoever did it where that is required, and stopped at every point where the decision
belongs to a human. It is the capability, not the machinery: it outlives any particular way of
carrying it out.""" ;
    biz:supports goal:accountable-delegation-with-peace-of-mind ;
    biz:ownedBy person:captain .

## Who answers for it.

person:captain
    a biz:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Captain" ;
    rdfs:comment """The human this organization exists to serve, and its default authority. The
capability is owned here because the decisions delegated work is not allowed to make stay with the
captain, and ownership is the model's word for who answers when one of them goes wrong.""" .

## Who it is delegated to.

agent:siana
    a biz:AgentIdentity ;
    rdfs:label "SIANA" ;
    rdfs:comment """The non-human actor the organization has put between the captain's intent and the
work that carries it out. It is modelled as an actor rather than as a mechanism because the
organization holds it to account the same way it holds a person: it is granted a role, it is given
work, and the work is attributable to it afterwards.""" ;
    biz:grantsRole role:fleet-orchestrator .

## What it is permitted to do.

role:fleet-orchestrator
    a biz:Role ;
    rdfs:label "Fleet orchestrator" ;
    rdfs:comment """Permission to run the interface between intent and delivery. Being asked to do
this work is not what makes it allowed; holding this role is, and that is why the permission is
written down separately from the assignment that exercises it.""" ;
    biz:permits cap:orchestrate-fleet-delivery .

## Under what rule.

policy:captain-governed-fleet-operation
    a biz:Policy ;
    rdfs:label "Captain-governed fleet operation" ;
    rdfs:comment """The captain is the default authority for every gate, and autonomy exists only
where the captain has explicitly granted it - never inferred from an earlier grant or from how
routine the work looks. Decisions only a human can make are put to the captain rather than taken.
Where independent validation is required, that validation is the acceptance boundary and work is not
accepted on the word of whoever produced it. Publishing work for review is never authority to merge
it: what lands is the captain's decision.""" .

## The work itself.

asg:operate-the-captains-fleet-interface
    a biz:Assignment ;
    rdfs:label "Operate the captain's fleet interface" ;
    rdfs:comment """The standing work SIANA is given: hold the layer between what the captain asks
for and what the fleet does, for as long as the organization wants the outcome above.""" ;
    biz:assignedTo agent:siana ;
    biz:targetsCapability cap:orchestrate-fleet-delivery ;
    biz:servesGoal goal:accountable-delegation-with-peace-of-mind ;
    biz:governedBy policy:captain-governed-fleet-operation .

